title: DuFour Sacks [+ chancellor +]!
subtitle: DuFour has turned on us...
view-if: (president == "DuFour" and not presidential_powers and marcher_in_government and ((dufour_angry >= 115 and not serannus_pending) or (dufour_angry >= 165 and serannus_pending)) and dufour_angry_trigger) and chancellor != "Askew" and next_election_time - time > 3 and not in_marcher_majority
priority: -1
new-page: true
on-arrival: gold_relation -= 8; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4 if chancellor_party != "Unionist"; pro_republic -= 3; pro_republic -= 1 if marcher_r >= 30; pro_republic -= 1 if weimar_coalition >= 50; coup_progress -= 1; dufour_sacked = 1; comeback_a = n_elections
go-to: bruning_right if (bruning_event_seen or year < 1930) and right_coalition >= 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7); bruning_center_right if (bruning_event_seen or year < 1930) and (center_right_coalition >= 50 and right_coalition < 50) and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7); bruning_chain if not ((bruning_event_seen or year < 1930) and right_coalition >= 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and not ((bruning_event_seen or year < 1930) and (center_right_coalition >= 50 and right_coalition < 50) and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7))
tags: event

= Chancellor [+ chancellor +] Sacked

President DuFour has made his dissatisfaction with the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> presence in government clear and has used his presidential powers to remove us by force. It seems like this decision wasn't a rash one, but rather a matter of finding the appropriate pretext to dismiss our government.

[? if marcher_votes >= 31:The <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> remaining electorally resilient despite the radicalizing effects of the economic depression has thwarted DuFour’s plan to burden us with governance and erode our popularity. Realizing his strategy has failed, he now moves to dismiss us from government to prevent further <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> reforms from fueling our rising support. ?][? if disfavored >= 15 or economic_growth < 0: the Commonwealth's economic crisis and our inadequate response have severely tested DuFour's patience, as he favors an austerity-driven approach. ?][? if royalist_votes >= 18: The rapid rise of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> in local elections has pushed DuFour to appoint a government more in line with the national mood. ?][? if rearmament_exposed or army_loyalty <= 0.1: Werner Staal and the Commonwealth Army, outraged by our actions, have leveraged their influence over DuFour to push for our removal. ?][? if capital_strike_progress >= 5: Business leaders, frustrated by our policies, have pressured DuFour’s inner circle to act against us. ?]

This is a blatant violation of democracy, but we are powerless to stop it. Our only hope is to rally enough support in the next election to reclaim our mandate. 

[? if started: (Dear player, PLEASE don't ragequit, toleration is completely changed from Red Autumn. You still have a chance.) ?]

@bruning_right
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; chancellor = "Askew"; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; justice_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "Gold"; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Unionist"; agriculture_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; in_right_coalition = 1; gold_right += 2; lvp_right += 2; liberal_cooperation -= 1; liberal_cooperation -= 3 if liberal_parliament > 0; liberal_parliament = 0 if liberal_parliament > 0; bourgeois_cooperation += 1

Replacing us is Edmund Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], who has reorganized his cabinet to encompass the right-wing parties, including the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": who reluctantly accede to DuFour's wishes for a government.?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":, who are happy to participate in such a coalition, to keep out the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> from government.?] Their coalition frustratingly holds a majority in the Assembly, meaning we are forced to accept the loss and prepare for the next elections.

[? if liberal_parliament == 1: The liberal parliamentary group has been broken apart due to the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> acting on its own accord. ?]

@bruning_center_right
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; justice_minister_party = ddp_name; justice_minister_party  = "LVP" if lvp_formed; justice_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "Gold"; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Unionist"; agriculture_minister_party = "Traditionalist"; in_center_right_coalition = 1; gold_right += 1; liberal_cooperation += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; ddp_right += 1; lvp_right += 1; bourgeois_cooperation += 2

Replacing us is Edmund Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], who has reorganized his cabinet to encompass the right-wing parties, including the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> who are happy to participate in such a coalition, to keep out the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> from government. Their coalition frustratingly holds a majority in the Assembly, meaning we are forced to accept the loss and prepare for the next elections.

@bruning_chain
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; minority_government = 1; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; bruning_event_timer = 6 if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930

Replacing us is Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], who has reorganized his cabinet to encompass the propertied parties. [? if bruning_event_seen or year < 1930: Although they lack a majority in the Assembly, we could tolerate their government at the next session to prevent new elections, effectively acquiescing to DuFour's wishes. ?][? if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930: New elections haven't been called yet but it's likely that they will be soon, considering Askew most likely doesn't have the majority of the Assembly behind him. ?]

- @tolerate
- @dont_tolerate

@tolerate
title: Oppose any votes of no confidence, voting for the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a propertied government.
view-if: bruning_event_seen or year < 1930
on-arrival: marcher_toleration = 1; left_dissent += 10; pro_republic -= 3; commons_collectivist += 3; commons_royalist += 3; commons_marcher -= 3; disfavored_collectivist += 5; disfavored_royalist += 3; disfavored_marcher -= 5; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 1; lvp_right += 2; liberal_cooperation += 1; welfare -= 2

Askew immediately begins to cut welfare using his emergency powers granted by President [+ president +]. We try to convince the workers that this policy is necessary in order to maintain a stable parliamentary government, and to deal with the fiscal consequences of the depression. Still, this policy provides excellent recruiting fodder for <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@dont_tolerate
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
view-if: bruning_event_seen or year < 1930
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 5
call: set_next_election_time

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].